{"content":[{"c":["HELDAI"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Baanah’s son, described as a Netophathite in the line of Othniel. He appears first as one of David’s mighty men (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.29","r":"2Sam.23.29","rawR":"2Sam.23.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.29","value":"2Sam.23.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 23:29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.30","r":"1Chr.11.30","rawR":"1Chr.11.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.30","value":"1Chr.11.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:30"},", “Heled”). In ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.15","r":"1Chr.27.15","rawR":"1Chr.27.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.15","value":"1Chr.27.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 27:15"},", he is called a commander of an army division of 24,000 that served during the 12th month of the year."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. One of the exiles returning from Babylon from whom the prophet Zechariah took gold and silver to make a crown for Joshua, the high priest (",{"href":"?bref=Zech.6.10","r":"Zech.6.10","rawR":"Zech.6.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zech.6.10","value":"Zech.6.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zec 6:10"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Heldai","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Sm 23:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.23.29","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.23.29","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.23.29"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 11:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.11.30","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.11.30","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.11.30"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 27:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.27.15","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.27.15","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.27.15"},{"anchorText":"Zec 6:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Zech.6.10","rawQueryValu